              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Added glycine, taurine, creatine or individual amino acids can raise the protein number a lab reports without adding intact protein. Read the full ingredient list, prefer brands that publish an amino acid table, and be skeptical of protein claims that look too good for the calories.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
