            Beef protein isolate is a real option for people who need to avoid dairy and eggs, or who follow a paleo or animal-based diet, but it is not powdered steak. Brands that publish their amino acid tables show a collagen-dominant profile with about 1 g of leucine per serving. Equip is the most transparent pick, Olympian Labs suits allergy-limited buyers who want no added collagen or aminos, and Carnivor has the widest flavor range.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you can eat eggs, egg white protein is the more complete dairy-free choice, and if you tolerate dairy, whey isolate is better value for muscle. Read the full ingredient list for added amino acids, pair beef shakes with leucine-rich meals, and if you have alpha-gal syndrome, kidney disease or a medical diet, check with your doctor or registered dietitian first.
